  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: e9620f8c34305754d8cc9a7e49e852d9, type: 3}
  m_Name: Subtitles_en-US
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_LocaleId:
    m_Code: en-US
  m_SharedData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 0eba1ca772668fc4495ea1112f65a946, type: 2}
  m_Metadata:
    m_Items: []
  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 236719157248
    m_Localized: '   '
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 1
    m_Localized: Glucagon
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 2
    m_Localized: You woke up late for physical education class...
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 3
    m_Localized: ' rushed out of the house and ended up not eating anything.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 4
    m_Localized: Since you arrived late, your teacher made you run around the field.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 5
    m_Localized: With the strenuous activity, and since you hadn't eaten properly,
      the glucose available in your blood was quickly consumed by the muscle cells.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 6
    m_Localized: As glucose is the main source of energy for cellular metabolism,
      you felt unwell, dizzy, and almost fainted.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 7
    m_Localized: This happens when the sugar concentration  in the bloodstream decreases
      much, entering a state of hypoglycemia.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 8
    m_Localized: We have a small deposit of glucose in some liver cells in the form
      of glycogen (which is a polymer of glucose molecules).
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 9
    m_Localized: Acid Hydrolase
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 10
    m_Localized: You had a bad flu and decided to go to the doctor.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 11
    m_Localized: He said there are many medicines for the flu, but none really cure
      it.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 12
    m_Localized: They only help to minimize symptoms such as headache and fever.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 13
    m_Localized: 'So you should follow these recommendations: take a rest; eat well
      and stay hydrated.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 14
    m_Localized: Wait for your defense system to fight the infectious agent.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 15
    m_Localized: Insulin
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 16
    m_Localized: Every time you have lunch at your grandmother's house, she makes
      a very good macaroni dish...
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 17
    m_Localized: and after a wonderful dessert
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 18
    m_Localized: You always eat so much that you leave there "too full."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 19
    m_Localized: Melanin
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 20
    m_Localized: You're at the beach enjoying a long weekend with friends.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 21
    m_Localized: The sun is very strong, and if you're not careful, you could get
      severely sunburned or even suffer from sunstroke (symptoms caused by excessive
      exposure to intense sunlight),
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 22
    m_Localized: 'Sunstroke causes: headache, nausea, vomiting, dizziness, blurred
      vision, mental confusion, which can lead to fainting.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 23
    m_Localized: 'Avoid this: don''t stay exposed to the sun for a long time, use
      sunscreen to avoid burning your skin.'
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 24
    m_Localized: Our skin produces melanin, which not only gives color to the skin,
      hair, and eyes,
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 25
    m_Localized: It also has the function of protecting our skin by filtering ultra
      violet rays, which can damage it
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 26
    m_Localized: The amount of melanin produced is determined genetically,
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 27
    m_Localized: the lighter the skin, the less melanin is produced,
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 28
    m_Localized: thus increasing susceptibility to sun damage.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 29
    m_Localized: Furthermore, frequent and long-term sun exposure can lead to the
      development of skin cancer.
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
